            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An electrolyte includes a fluorinated cyclic carbonate, and a multi-nitrile compound having an ether bond. Based on the total weight of the electrolyte, a weight percentage (Cf) of the fluorinated cyclic carbonate is greater than a weight percentage (Cn) of themulti-nitrile compound having the ether bond; and 1&lt; Cf / Cn ≤ 3 or 5.5&lt; Cf / Cn ≤ 20. The electrolyte of the present application can control the expansion of the electrochemical device, so that the electrochemical device has excellent cycle, storage and/or floating-charge performance.</p>
            </abstract>
